1
00:02:31,067 --> 00:02:41,067
All pirates searching for the treasure One Piece must brave the second half of the Grand Line.

2
00:02:41,067 --> 00:02:45,067
These wild and dangerous seas are known as the New World.

3
00:02:45,067 --> 00:02:52,067
Gold Roger and his crew were the only men to ever chart these waters and learn all the secrets they held.

4
00:02:52,067 --> 00:02:59,067
For the rest of the pirates of the world, this has proven to be the end of the world, a graveyard of dreams.

5
00:02:59,067 --> 00:03:09,067
Now, Monkey D. Luffy, a boy whose body became rubber after eating the gum gum fruit, sets sail into the New World with his faithful crew.

6
00:03:09,067 --> 00:03:13,067
I will be the king of the pirates!

7
00:03:16,067 --> 00:03:25,067
During their journey to the New World, Luffy and his crew arrive on Fishman Island, which is located 10,000 meters below sea level.

8
00:03:25,067 --> 00:03:32,067
The Fishman Pirates, led by Horty Jones and assisted by Vander Decken, plot to overthrow King Neptune.

9
00:03:32,067 --> 00:03:38,067
It is not long before the Straw Hats get pulled into the conflict and find themselves in the midst of an all-out war.

10
00:03:38,067 --> 00:03:45,067
After a change of plans, Horty threatens to crush the entire island under the weight of a massive ship.

11
00:03:45,067 --> 00:03:48,067
Either way, the whole island is doomed!

12
00:03:48,067 --> 00:03:52,067
That includes your friends, the princess, and everyone else down there!

13
00:03:52,067 --> 00:03:57,067
You're just a weakling, get it? You can't protect anyone!

14
00:03:57,067 --> 00:04:02,067
Watch me! I'll save them all!

15
00:04:02,067 --> 00:04:06,067
I've trained for two years! I'm ready!

16
00:04:06,067 --> 00:04:15,067
A massive, confused fight! The Straw Hats versus the new Fishman Pirates!

17
00:04:15,067 --> 00:04:38,067
You think you can save them all? Oh, that's rich. You talk a big game, don't you, Straw Hat?

18
00:04:38,067 --> 00:04:48,067
This is crazy! He turned his back on Decken, too?

19
00:04:48,067 --> 00:04:53,067
Sister! Swim away! It's up to you to save our people, Shirahoshi!

20
00:04:57,067 --> 00:04:59,067
It's a bit late for that.

21
00:04:59,067 --> 00:05:09,067
A bit late? What is that supposed to mean?

22
00:05:09,067 --> 00:05:14,067
Donut! Isn't Decken on the brink of death right now?

23
00:05:14,067 --> 00:05:19,067
If he dies or passes out, then no one goes back to normal, right?

24
00:05:29,067 --> 00:05:41,067
He's power will go away, and the ship will stop following her!

25
00:05:42,067 --> 00:05:44,067
And that means... that...

26
00:05:46,067 --> 00:05:48,067
It'll hit the island!

27
00:05:51,067 --> 00:05:55,067
Why'd you kick me? That hurt!

28
00:05:55,067 --> 00:05:58,067
Suck it up! I'll kick you as many times as it takes!

29
00:05:58,067 --> 00:06:00,067
You're such a meaty!

30
00:06:01,067 --> 00:06:04,067
Even the captain would have kicked me for no reason!

31
00:06:06,067 --> 00:06:08,067
Well, you shouldn't have hurt Nami.

32
00:06:09,067 --> 00:06:10,067
You big waste of space.

33
00:06:13,067 --> 00:06:15,067
How about another goose egg to match?

34
00:06:16,067 --> 00:06:17,067
No! Get away!

35
00:06:17,067 --> 00:06:22,067
Next time, be careful!

36
00:06:23,067 --> 00:06:25,067
Where you drop your fat ass!

37
00:06:32,067 --> 00:06:33,067
Nami!

38
00:06:35,067 --> 00:06:38,067
Please don't get any scratches on that hot body!

39
00:06:40,067 --> 00:06:41,067
Not another one!

40
00:06:42,067 --> 00:06:43,067
Give me a break!

41
00:06:44,067 --> 00:06:45,067
Watch out! She's dangerous!

42
00:06:45,067 --> 00:06:49,067
Last time she used that magic wand thing, she did some major damage!

43
00:06:51,067 --> 00:06:52,067
Ha! Black Ball!

44
00:06:57,067 --> 00:06:58,067
What's she doing there?

45
00:06:59,067 --> 00:07:00,067
She must be some kind of witch!

46
00:07:00,067 --> 00:07:02,067
A witch? That's rude, you guys!

47
00:07:03,067 --> 00:07:04,067
Hm.

48
00:07:05,067 --> 00:07:07,067
How about Enchantress? That's much nicer!

49
00:07:07,067 --> 00:07:16,067
But it's not magic! More like advanced meteorology, you might say!

50
00:07:20,067 --> 00:07:21,067
Ah! Uh-oh!

51
00:07:21,067 --> 00:07:22,067
Uh-oh!

52
00:07:22,067 --> 00:07:23,067
Squirt Cloud Rod, go!

53
00:07:23,067 --> 00:07:24,067
Ah!

54
00:07:24,067 --> 00:07:25,067
Ah!

55
00:07:33,067 --> 00:07:34,067
Ah!

56
00:07:35,067 --> 00:07:36,067
What the?

57
00:07:36,067 --> 00:07:37,067
Help me, I'm dying!

58
00:07:38,067 --> 00:07:39,067
Stay back!

59
00:07:39,067 --> 00:07:40,067
I can't let you touch me, hee!

60
00:07:41,067 --> 00:07:42,067
Or I'll be dried squid!

61
00:07:42,067 --> 00:07:43,067
Go ahead!

62
00:07:43,067 --> 00:07:44,067
Icarus!

63
00:07:45,067 --> 00:07:50,067
Did you notice how distraught the black-suited buffoon was when that woman fell to the ground?

64
00:07:51,067 --> 00:07:52,067
I believe...

65
00:07:53,067 --> 00:07:54,067
We may have discovered his weakness.

66
00:07:55,067 --> 00:07:56,067
Oh yeah!

67
00:07:57,067 --> 00:07:58,067
I'll make sure she can't move.

68
00:07:59,067 --> 00:08:00,067
You can do the gruesome part!

69
00:08:01,067 --> 00:08:02,067
Leave it to me, hee!

70
00:08:03,067 --> 00:08:06,067
See, if you don't want to get yourself zapped, you shouldn't be playing with lightning.

71
00:08:07,067 --> 00:08:08,067
Ah!

72
00:08:09,067 --> 00:08:10,067
Hey!

73
00:08:11,067 --> 00:08:12,067
